{"metadata":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"FloatingPointFormatStyle"}],"modules":[{"name":"FoundationInternationalization"}],"symbolKind":"struct","externalID":"s:30FoundationInternationalization24FloatingPointFormatStyleV","roleHeading":"Structure","role":"symbol","title":"FloatingPointFormatStyle","platforms":[{"beta":false,"deprecated":false,"name":"iOS","introducedAt":"15.0","unavailable":false},{"beta":false,"deprecated":false,"name":"iPadOS","introducedAt":"15.0","unavailable":false},{"beta":false,"deprecated":false,"name":"Mac Catalyst","introducedAt":"15.0","unavailable":false},{"beta":false,"deprecated":false,"name":"macOS","introducedAt":"12.0","unavailable":false},{"beta":false,"deprecated":false,"name":"tvOS","introducedAt":"15.0","unavailable":false},{"beta":false,"deprecated":false,"name":"watchOS","introducedAt":"8.0","unavailable":false}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"FloatingPointFormatStyle"}]},"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/20FoundationEssentials11FormatStyleP","doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/20FoundationEssentials20ParseableFormatStyleP","doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/Se","doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/SE","doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/SQ","doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/SH","doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/s16SendableMetatypeP","doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/17_StringProcessing29CustomConsumingRegexComponentP","doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/17_StringProcessing14RegexComponentP"],"type":"conformsTo"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"FloatingPointFormatStyle","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Value","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Value","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BinaryFloatingPoint","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SB"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Instances of "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/documentation\/FoundationInternationalization\/FloatingPointFormatStyle"},{"type":"text","text":" create localized, human-readable text from "},{"type":"text","text":"doc:\/\/com.apple.documentation\/documentation\/swift\/binaryfloatingpoint"},{"type":"text","text":" numbers and parse string representations of numbers into instances of "},{"type":"text","text":"doc:\/\/com.apple.documentation\/documentation\/swift\/binaryfloatingpoint"},{"type":"text","text":" types. All of the Swift standard library’s floating-point types, such as "},{"type":"text","text":"doc:\/\/com.apple.documentation\/documentation\/swift\/double"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"text","text":"doc:\/\/com.apple.documentation\/documentation\/swift\/float"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"text","text":"doc:\/\/com.apple.documentation\/documentation\/swift\/float80"},{"type":"text","text":", conform to "},{"type":"text","text":"doc:\/\/com.apple.documentation\/documentation\/swift\/binaryfloatingpoint"},{"type":"text","text":", and therefore work with this format style."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/documentation\/FoundationInternationalization\/FloatingPointFormatStyle","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" includes two nested types, ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/documentation\/FoundationInternationalization\/FloatingPointFormatStyle\/Percent","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/documentation\/FoundationInternationalization\/FloatingPointFormatStyle\/Currency","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", for working with percentages and currencies, respectively. Each format style includes a configuration that determines how it represents numeric values, for things like grouping, displaying signs, and variant presentations like scientific notation. ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/documentation\/FoundationInternationalization\/FloatingPointFormatStyle","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/documentation\/FoundationInternationalization\/FloatingPointFormatStyle\/Percent","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" include a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/documentation\/FoundationInternationalization\/NumberFormatStyleConfiguration","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/documentation\/FoundationInternationalization\/FloatingPointFormatStyle\/Currency","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" includes a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/documentation\/FoundationInternationalization\/CurrencyFormatStyleConfiguration","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":". You can customize numeric formatting for a style by adjusting its backing configuration. The system automatically caches unique configurations of a format style to enhance performance."}]},{"style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Foundation provides another format style type, ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/documentation\/FoundationInternationalization\/IntegerFormatStyle","type":"reference"},{"text":", for working with numbers that conform to ","type":"text"},{"text":"doc:\/\/com.apple.documentation\/documentation\/swift\/binaryinteger","type":"text"},{"text":". For Foundation’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"Decimal","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" type, use ","type":"text"},{"code":"Decimal\/FormatStyle","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}],"name":"Note","type":"aside"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Formatting-floating-point-values","text":"Formatting floating-point values","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Use the ","type":"text"},{"text":"doc:\/\/com.apple.documentation\/documentation\/swift\/binaryfloatingpoint\/formatted()","type":"text"},{"text":" method to create a string representation of a floating-point value using the default ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/documentation\/FoundationInternationalization\/FloatingPointFormatStyle"},{"text":" configuration.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let formattedDefault = 12345.67.formatted()","\/\/ formattedDefault is \"12,345.67\" in the en_US locale.","\/\/ Other locales may use different separator and grouping behavior."],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"You can specify a format style by providing an argument to the ","type":"text"},{"text":"doc:\/\/com.apple.documentation\/documentation\/swift\/binaryfloatingpoint\/formatted(_:)-4ksqj","type":"text"},{"text":" method. The following example shows the number ","type":"text"},{"code":"0.1","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" represented in each of the available styles, in the ","type":"text"},{"code":"en_US","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" locale:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let number = 0.1","","let formattedNumber = number.formatted(.number)","\/\/ formattedNumber is \"0.1\".","","let formattedPercent = number.formatted(.percent)","\/\/ formattedPercent is \"10%\".","","let formattedCurrency = number.formatted(.currency(code: \"USD\"))","\/\/ formattedCurrency is \"$0.10\"."],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each style provides methods for updating its numeric configuration, including the number of significant digits, grouping length, and more. You can specify a numeric configuration by calling as many of these methods as you need in any order you choose. The following example shows the same number with default and custom configurations:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let exampleNumber = 123456.78","","let defaultFormatting = exampleNumber.formatted(.number)","\/\/ defaultFormatting is \"123 456,78\" for the \"fr_FR\" locale.","\/\/ defaultFormatting is \"123,456.78\" for the \"en_US\" locale.","","let customFormatting = exampleNumber.formatted(",".number",".grouping(.never)",".sign(strategy: .always()))","\/\/ customFormatting is \"+123456.78\""],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Creating-a-floating-point-format-style-instance","text":"Creating a floating-point format style instance","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The previous examples use static factory methods like ","type":"text"},{"code":"FormatStyle\/number-8c8rj","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to create format styles within the call to the ","type":"text"},{"text":"doc:\/\/com.apple.documentation\/documentation\/swift\/binaryfloatingpoint\/formatted(_:)-4ksqj","type":"text"},{"text":" method. You can also create a ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/documentation\/FoundationInternationalization\/FloatingPointFormatStyle"},{"text":" instance and use it to repeatedly format different values, with the ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/documentation\/FoundationInternationalization\/FloatingPointFormatStyle\/format(_:)"},{"text":" method:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let percentFormatStyle = FloatingPointFormatStyle<Double>.Percent()","","percentFormatStyle.format(0.5) \/\/ \"50%\"","percentFormatStyle.format(0.855) \/\/ \"85.5%\"","percentFormatStyle.format(1.0) \/\/ \"100%\"",""],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Parsing-floating-point-values","text":"Parsing floating-point values","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"You can use ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/documentation\/FoundationInternationalization\/FloatingPointFormatStyle"},{"text":" to parse strings into floating-point values. You can define the format style within the type’s initializer or pass in a format style created outside the function, as shown here:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let price = try? Double(\"$3,500.63\",","format: .currency(code: \"USD\")) \/\/ 3500.63","","let priceFormatStyle = FloatingPointFormatStyle<Double>.Currency(code: \"USD\")","let salePrice = try? Double(\"$731.67\",","format: priceFormatStyle) \/\/ 731.67"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Matching-regular-expressions","text":"Matching regular expressions","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Along with parsing numeric values in strings, you can use theSwift regular expression domain-specific language to match and capture numeric substrings. The following example defines a percentage format style to match a percentage value using ","type":"text"},{"code":"en_US","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" numeric conventions. The rest of the regular expression ignores any characters prior to a ","type":"text"},{"code":"\": \"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" sequence that precedes the percentage substring.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import RegexBuilder","let source = \"Percentage complete: 55.1%\"","let matcher = Regex {","OneOrMore(.any)","\": \"","Capture {","One(.localizedDoublePercentage(locale: Locale(identifier: \"en_US\")))","}","}","let match = source.firstMatch(of: matcher)","let localizedPercentage = match?.1","print(\"\\(localizedPercentage!)\") \/\/ 0.551"],"type":"codeListing"}],"kind":"content"}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/documentation\/FoundationInternationalization\/FloatingPointFormatStyle\/Attributed-swift.struct","doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/documentation\/FoundationInternationalization\/FloatingPointFormatStyle\/Currency","doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/documentation\/FoundationInternationalization\/FloatingPointFormatStyle\/Percent"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Structures"},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers","title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/documentation\/FoundationInternationalization\/FloatingPointFormatStyle\/init(from:)","doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/documentation\/FoundationInternationalization\/FloatingPointFormatStyle\/init(locale:)"]},{"title":"Instance Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/documentation\/FoundationInternationalization\/FloatingPointFormatStyle\/attributed-swift.property","doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/documentation\/FoundationInternationalization\/FloatingPointFormatStyle\/locale"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Properties"},{"title":"Instance Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/documentation\/FoundationInternationalization\/FloatingPointFormatStyle\/decimalSeparator(strategy:)","doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/documentation\/FoundationInternationalization\/FloatingPointFormatStyle\/grouping(_:)","doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/documentation\/FoundationInternationalization\/FloatingPoint